    "profile_text": {
        "body": "NVIDIA is a public company, traded as NVDA and registered under CIK 0001045810, founded in 1993 and headquartered in Santa Clara, California. Its most recent 10-K, for a period ending 2026-01-25, reported revenue of $215,938,000,000.\n\nPer its own site, NVIDIA's AI work centers on the Nemotron family of multimodal open models, which the company describes as built for agentic reasoning in graduate-level science, advanced math, and visual understanding, and as efficient enough for long-running, self-evolving agents. The site names Nemotron 3.5 Lightning for specialized tasks and NeMo Switchyard for routing each step to the right model. Nemotron models are offered as NVIDIA NIM microservices for deployment, which the company says requires an NVIDIA AI Enterprise license, and are also published under the NVIDIA Open Model License, described as permissive and allowing commercial use and modification without crediting NVIDIA. The site lists speech models for automatic speech recognition, text-to-speech, and neural machine translation, plus Retriever models for document understanding and embeddings. Supporting tools named include NVIDIA NeMo, NVIDIA Blueprints, NVIDIA Dynamo, TensorRT-LLM, NIM, SGLang, and vLLM, with platform support cited for NVIDIA RTX PRO and NVIDIA DGX Spark. Bryan Catanzaro, VP of applied deep learning research at NVIDIA, is quoted on the vision behind Nemotron, and ServiceNow is named among ecosystem partners.\n\nOn the legal side, the record counts 220 cases in California.",
